---
import LabLayout from "../../layouts/LabLayout.astro";

const comparisons = [
  {
    id: "production-wasp",
    title: "Production plasma thrust",
    view: "Follow 1.6×",
  },
  {
    id: "reference-wasp",
    title: "Accepted study thrust reference",
    view: "Follow 1.6×",
  },
  { id: "scout", title: "Scout: paired plasma engines", view: "Follow 4×" },
  { id: "corvette", title: "Corvette: five plasma engines", view: "Follow 4×" },
];
const phases = [
  { id: "charge", title: "Charge", seconds: "0.1" },
  { id: "release", title: "Release", seconds: "0.25" },
  { id: "thrust", title: "Sustained thrust", seconds: "0.8" },
  { id: "restart", title: "Later release at speed", seconds: "5.4" },
];
---

<LabLayout title="Plasma thrust comparison" wide>
  <p class="context">
    Static comparison captured 20 November 2026 before retiring the
    <a href="/lab/studies/plasma-light-2026-11-11#charge-feel"
      >plasma light study’s</a
    >
    live apparatus. These images show the code available at retirement, not the
    original 11 November evidence or a new acceptance of the study’s proposals.
  </p>
  <p class="context">
    All four scenes use burn B1 from rest, no randomness, and a 0.2 s plasma
    charge. The Wasp has one Plasma main engine and ion stabilizers; its
    production light and accepted study painter are captured at matching times
    in Follow 1.6×. The Scout has two side Plasma engines; the Corvette has two
    side and three aft Plasma engines. Both use production light in Follow 4×.
    These scenes retained the production background available at retirement,
    unlike the study’s historical Canvas background. No controls or simulation
    run on this page.
  </p>
  <div class="comparisons">
    {comparisons.map((comparison) => (
      <section>
        <h2>{comparison.title}</h2>
        <p>{comparison.view}</p>
        {phases.map((phase) => (
          <figure>
            <img
              src={`/studies/plasma-light-2026-11-11/comparison-${comparison.id}-${phase.id}.png`}
              alt={`${comparison.title}: ${phase.title.toLowerCase()} at ${phase.seconds} seconds`}
              width="1190"
              height="669"
              loading="lazy"
            />
            <figcaption>
              {phase.title} · {phase.seconds} s
            </figcaption>
          </figure>
        ))}
      </section>
    ))}
  </div>
  <p class="context">
    The fixed-flight sequence preserves charge, release, sustained light and a
    later release with accumulated residue. It does not test feel under manual
    control or certify the look on other fittings. The Scout and Corvette images
    are retained comparison conditions, not additional study decisions.
  </p>
</LabLayout>

<style>
.context {
  max-width: 72ch;
  margin-block: var(--spacing-lg);
}
.comparisons {
  display: grid;
  grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
  gap: var(--spacing-xl);
}
.context a {
  color: var(--color-action);
}
h2 {
  line-height: 1.2;
  min-height: 2.4em;
}
figure {
  margin: var(--spacing-lg) 0;
}
img {
  display: block;
  width: 100%;
  height: auto;
}
figcaption {
  margin-top: var(--spacing-sm);
  color: var(--color-text-muted);
  font-size: var(--font-size-caption);
}
</style>
